000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000qj\u0000\u0000docProps/core.xmlPK\u0001\u0002-\u0000\u0014\u0000\u0006\u0000\b\u0000\u0000\u0000!\u0000��]�z\u0002\u0000\u00006\u000b\u0000\u0000\u0012\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Dm\u0000\u0000word/fontTable.xmlPK\u0001\u0002-\u0000\u0014\u0000\u0006\u0000\b\u0000\u0000\u0000!\u0000\u0012�<�9\u0002\u0000\u0000\u0006\u001e\u0000\u0000\u0014\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000�o\u0000\u0000word/webSettings.xmlPK\u0001\u0002-\u0000\u0014\u0000\u0006\u0000\b\u0000\u0000\u0000!\u0000~�s��\u0001\u0000\u0000�\u0003\u0000\u0000\u0010\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Yr\u0000\u0000docProps/app.xmlPK\u0005\u0006\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0014\u0000\u0014\u0000\r\u0005\u0000\u0000u\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000","minutes_text":"PERMITS AND LICENSES COMMITTEE\n  MINUTES\n  February 14, 2019\n\nA meeting of the Permits and License Committee was held on Thursday, February 14,\n2019, at 2:05 pm in the City Council Community Room A, 1st Floor\n\nRoll Call:  Members Present:  Harjinder Singh, Administration\n  Yvonne Horton, City Clerk\n  Cpt. Reggie Johnson, LACO Fire Department\n  Eddy Ikemefuna, Planning & Building Department\n\n  Staff Present:  Peggy L. Velasquez, Finance Department\n  Serena Martinez, Finance Department\n\nPublic Comments Regarding Agenda Items\nDuring public comments any person may address the Permits & License Committee,\nprovided the item is within the subject matter jurisdiction of the Permits & License\nCommittee.\nChairman Singh asked if there were any persons present who wished to address the\nPermits & License Committee on any item on the Agenda.\nChairman Singh reported that there were no public requests to speak.\n\nA motion was moved and seconded to approve the minutes from the meeting held on\nNovember 21, 2018 and January 10, 2019. Minutes from the meetings on January 24\nand 31, 2019 were not included in the packet.\n\nItem #1:  A motion was moved and seconded to APPROVE the business license\n  request for Stephanie Point and Gregory C. Kim; dba: Point 2 Point Global\n  Security, Inc., provide security guard service at Home Depot, 3363 W.\n  Century Blvd., subject to payment of annual business license renewal and\n  tax fees; provide list of all prospective employees and include valid\n  government-issued identification and applicable State Bureau of Security\n  and Investigative Services working within the City; a list of registered and\n  insured vehicles to be used and if applicable list of locations where services\n  will be rendered; business owner cannot employ 290 PC registrants or any\n  persons that may pose a threat to the safety of patrons or the general\n  public; adhere to all applicable IMC regulations, including noise and\n  signage. Motion carried unanimously. (Activity No. 00273302)\n\n  Present: Greg Kim, Director, California Operations\n  Alfredo Barocio, Assistant Operation Manager\n\nItem #2:  The Planning Department informed the Permits & License Committee that\n  Ken Williams and John Williams; dba: Universal College of Beauty, Inc., is\n  not required to go through the Permits & License process to operate a\n  beauty school at 244 N. Market St. (Activity No. 00273304)\n\fPermits & License Committee  February 14, 2019\nMinutes  Page 2 of 4\n\nItem #3:  A motion was moved and seconded to APPROVE the business license\n  renewal request for Garegin Khachatryan; South Park Doggie LAX\n  Boarding and Daycare to operate an animal facility at 8613 Aviation Blvd.,\n  subject to payment of annual business license and tax fees; provide current\n  applicable state licensing; provide valid government-issued identification\n  for all employees; maintain a clean and sanitized facility at all times to\n  ensure health and safety of all animals being serviced or housed at the\n  establishment; facility is subject to inspection by an police, code\n  enforcement or animal control officer at any time of day or night; improper\n  disposal of waste products of any kind is strictly prohibited; in the interest\n  of public and animal safety, this establishment is not permitted shall not\n  employ or have any person in the business that may pose a safety risk to\n  persons or animals (i.e. any person with prior convictions for any crimes\n  against animals); adhere to all IMC rules and regulations, including noise,\n  signage, state, federal and local laws. (Activity No. 00249941)\n\n  Present: Sesilia Candido, Personal Assistant to Garegin Khachatryan\n\nItem #4:  A motion was moved and seconded to APPROVE the tobacco retailer\n  license request for Anisa Shah; dba: Sharif’s Smoke Shop to operate as a\n  tobacco retailer at 151 W. Manchester Blvd., subject to sales of single\n  cigarettes is strictly prohibited; sales of tobacco, hookah, vapor and e-\n  cigarette products to minors, under age 21 is strictly prohibited; persons\n  purchasing tobacco or any related tobacco products shall have valid\n  identification on their person at all times to enforce laws restricting\n  underage access to tobacco use, including hookah products; “NO\n  LOITERING,” “NO TRESSPASSING,” and “NO PANHANDLING” signage\n  must be posted outside of the business; sales of marijuana and cannabis\n  products, narcotics and narcotics paraphernalia, i.e., any type of pipe used\n  to ingest other narcotics such as base “crack” cocaine, methamphetamine,\n  including glass cylindrical tube and bubble shaped pipes used to smoke\n  and/or ingest narcotics; sales of Tobacco pipes is permitted; sales or\n  display of any type of weapons, i.e., clubs, swords, knives, pepper spray,\n  Taser/Stun guns is strictly prohibited; Tobacco Retailer business owners\n  and/or new applicants or their designees is subject to random Permits &\n  Licensing establishment inspections at any time of the day or night by any\n  Police and Code Enforcement officers; purpose of random inspections is\n  to enforce business establishments adhere to the regulations set forth by\n  the City of Inglewood and for Community Public Health & Safety; parties,\n  social events or gatherings of any type is strictly prohibited; music boxes,\n  live bands/music, disc jockeys (DJ’s), etc., is strictly prohibited; business\n  owner(s) is required to operate within normal business hours; adhere to all\n  applicable IMC rules and regulations, including noise and signage. Motion\n  carried unanimously. (Activity No. 00272723)\n\fPermits & License Committee  February 14, 2019\nMinutes  Page 3 of 4\n\nItem #5:  A motion was moved and seconded to collectively APPROVE the following\n  business license renewals as recommended:\n\n  Business Name  Activity No.  Business Name  Activity No.\n  1  Close Up Kutts  00249772  17  Rainbow Nails  00249927\n  2  Minion Soft Serve Ice Cream  00249929  18  End Results Hair Salon  00249828\n  3  TGA Casa De Ada  00249878  19  Diego's Salon  00249768\n  4  The Lounge Barbershop  00249769  20  The Hertz Coporation  00249716\n  5  Eleven Twenty LLC  00249920  21  Big C Jewelry & Loan, LLc  00249962\n  6  TLC Hair Salon  00249852  22  La Brea Nails  00249825\n  G4S Security Solutions (USA)\n  7  Romero's Beauty Salon  00249845  23  Inc.  00249807\n  8  Lawles Enterprises, Inc.  00249791  24  Satelite Travel  00249990\n  9  LFT Nail Ssalon  00249824  25  Real Rich Hair Studio  00249907\n  Americare Group, Inc.;\n 10  Q Nails  00249872  26  Westchester Villa  00249984\n 11  Today Nails #2  00249812  27  Nail Dega  00249897\n 12  Cinderella's Beauty Salon  00249827  28  TBH International, LLC  00249949\n  Foreign Car Repair Inc.; dba:\n 13  New Image Barbershop  00249774  29  foreign Car Repair and Sales  00249742\n  Southern California\n 14  MG Parking  00249972  30  Ambulance, Inc.  00249682\n 15  Pretty Nails  00249849  31  Mamabama Exotic Autos  00249751\n  Centinela Skilled Nursing &\n  Wellness\n 16  American Nails  00249821  32  Centre West, LLC  00249961\n\n  Subject to payment of business tax; adhere to all applicable IMC\n  regulations, including noise and signage. Motion carried unanimously.\n\nItem #6:  A motion was moved and seconded to collectively APPROVE the following\n  tobacco retailer license renewals as recommended:\n\n  Business Name  Activity No.  Business Name  Activity No.\n 1  S&H Liquor  00250350  6  Rite Aide Corporation  00250360\n  SK Market Inc.; dba:\n 2  Best Bargain  00250271  7  La Brea Liquor  00250311\n 3  J & F Oil Corp.  00250362  8  Liquor Warehouse  00250282\n  JKG Food Mart, Inc; dba:  PNS, Inc; dba: Forum\n 4  San's Liquor  00250348  9  Liquor  00250354\n 5  Costco Wholesale #769  00250277\n\n  subject to sales of single cigarettes is strictly prohibited; sales of tobacco,\n  hookah, vapor and e-cigarette products to minors, under age 21 is strictly\n  prohibited; persons purchasing tobacco or any related tobacco products\n  shall have valid identification on their person at all times to enforce laws\n  restricting underage access to tobacco use, including hookah products;\n  “NO LOITERING,” “NO TRESSPASSING,” and “NO PANHANDLING”\n  signage must be posted outside of the business; sales of marijuana and\n\fPermits & License Committee  February 14, 2019\nMinutes  Page 4 of 4\n\n  cannabis products, narcotics and narcotics paraphernalia, i.e., any type of\n  pipe used to ingest other narcotics such as base “crack” cocaine,\n  methamphetamine, including glass cylindrical tube and bubble shaped\n  pipes used to smoke and/or ingest narcotics; sales of Tobacco pipes is\n  permitted; sales or display of any type of weapons, i.e., clubs, swords,\n  knives, pepper spray, Taser/Stun guns is strictly prohibited; Tobacco\n  Retailer business owners and/or new applicants or their designees is\n  subject to random Permits & Licensing establishment inspections at any\n  time of the day or night by any Police and Code Enforcement officers;\n  purpose of random inspections is to enforce business establishments\n  adhere to the regulations set forth by the City of Inglewood and for\n  Community Public Health & Safety; parties, social events or gatherings of\n  any type is strictly prohibited; music boxes, live bands/music, disc jockeys\n  (DJ’s), etc., is strictly prohibited; business owner(s) is required to operate\n  within normal business hours; adhere to all applicable IMC rules and\n  regulations, including noise and signage. Motion carried unanimously.\n\nThere being no further business, the meeting was adjourned at 2:20 p.m.\n\n  Respectfully submitted,\n  Peggy L. Velasquez, Recording Secretary","tries":1}